/-!
# The Kac–Moody algebra of a realization, by generators and relations

Let `A` be a square matrix of integers and `R` a realization of `A` over a field `K`
(`TauCeti.CartanRealization`): simple coroots `hᵢ` in a `K`-vector space `H` and simple roots
`αᵢ` in its dual with `αⱼ(hᵢ) = Aᵢⱼ`. This file defines the Lie algebra generated by the whole
space `H` together with elements `eᵢ`, `fᵢ`, subject to

* `H` is abelian, `⁅h, eⱼ⁆ = αⱼ(h) eⱼ` and `⁅h, fⱼ⁆ = -αⱼ(h) fⱼ` for `h ∈ H`;
* `⁅eᵢ, fᵢ⁆ = hᵢ` and `⁅eᵢ, fⱼ⁆ = 0` for `i ≠ j`;
* Serre's relations `(ad eᵢ) ^ (-Aᵢⱼ) ⁅eᵢ, eⱼ⁆ = 0` and `(ad fᵢ) ^ (-Aᵢⱼ) ⁅fᵢ, fⱼ⁆ = 0`.

Over a field of characteristic zero, for a symmetrizable generalized Cartan matrix and a minimal
realization, this is the Kac–Moody algebra `𝔤(A)` of Kac's book, by the Gabber–Kac theorem
[Kac, Theorem 9.11], which is not proved here and is not claimed in other characteristics; a
larger realization adds central directions. For a generalized Cartan matrix and `i ≠ j`
the last relations are `(ad eᵢ) ^ (1 - Aᵢⱼ) eⱼ = 0` and its lowering analogue; the exponent is
truncated at zero exactly as in Mathlib's `Matrix.ToLieAlgebra`, so that the derived algebra below
is compared with that presentation relator by relator.

Unlike `Matrix.ToLieAlgebra`, which only has the generators `hᵢ`, `eᵢ`, `fᵢ` and presents the
derived algebra, this presentation uses the full realization. That is what makes the simple roots
linearly independent characters of `H` even when `A` is singular, as in affine type. The space `H`
enters through free generators indexed by its elements, and the linearity of `h ↦ h` is imposed by
relators, so that `TauCeti.KacMoody.cartanElement` is a linear map.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.KacMoody.IsAuxRelator` and `TauCeti.KacMoody.IsRelator`: the Cartan-linearity, Chevalley,
  and Serre defining relators in the free Lie algebra.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.auxIdeal` and `TauCeti.KacMoody.presentationIdeal`: the Lie ideals of the free
  Lie algebra generated by the auxiliary and full defining relators.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.PresentedLieAlgebra`: the quotient of the free Lie algebra by
  `TauCeti.KacMoody.presentationIdeal`.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.cartanElement`, `TauCeti.KacMoody.positiveGenerator` and
  `TauCeti.KacMoody.negativeGenerator`: the images of the generators.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.SatisfiesAuxRelations` and `TauCeti.KacMoody.SatisfiesRelations`: a linear map
  on `H` and two families of elements of a Lie algebra satisfying the auxiliary and full defining
  relations.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.lift`: the homomorphism out of the presented algebra determined by such data.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.chevalleyInvolution`: the involutive Chevalley automorphism acting as `-1` on
  `H` and exchanging `eᵢ` with `-fᵢ`.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.positiveSubalgebra` and `TauCeti.KacMoody.negativeSubalgebra`: the Lie
  subalgebras `n⁺` and `n⁻` generated by the `eᵢ` and by the `fᵢ`.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.positiveQuotientHom` and `TauCeti.KacMoody.negativeQuotientHom`: the canonical
  homomorphisms `FreeLieAlgebra K I ⧸ serreIdeal K A →ₗ⁅K⁆ PresentedLieAlgebra R`.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.serreHom`: the homomorphism from `Matrix.ToLieAlgebra K A` sending its
  generators to `cartanElement R hᵢ`, `eᵢ` and `fᵢ`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.KacMoody.lift_cartanElement` and its companions, with `TauCeti.KacMoody.hom_ext` and
  `TauCeti.KacMoody.equiv_ext`: the universal property of the presentation.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.lieSpan_generators_eq_top`: the generators generate the presented algebra.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.cartanElement_mem_center` and `TauCeti.KacMoody.cartanElement_mem_center_iff`:
  vectors in `R.cartanCenter` map into the center of `𝔤`, and when `cartanElement R` is injective
  these are the only central Cartan vectors.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.range_positiveQuotientHom` and `TauCeti.KacMoody.range_negativeQuotientHom`:
  the ranges of the quotient maps are `positiveSubalgebra` and `negativeSubalgebra`.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.range_serreHom_sup_range_cartanElement`: `𝔤 = 𝔤' + H`, where `𝔤'` is the
  image of `Matrix.ToLieAlgebra K A`.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.range_serreHom_eq_derivedSeries`: that image is the derived algebra `⁅𝔤, 𝔤⁆`.
* `TauCeti.KacMoody.lie_ad_pow_lie_eq_zero`: for a generalized Cartan matrix, the lowering
  generators kill the raising Serre elements in any Lie algebra where the Chevalley
  generator-bracket identities hold (Kac, §3.3).

## References

* V. G. Kac, *Infinite-dimensional Lie algebras*, third edition, §1.2 (the auxiliary algebra on
  a realization), §1.3 (the algebra `𝔤(A)`, its derived algebra and `𝔤(A) = 𝔤'(A) + 𝔥`), §3.3
  (Serre elements commute with opposite generators), and Theorem 9.11 (the presentation of `𝔤(A)`
  by Serre's relations in the symmetrizable case, stated over the complex numbers and used here
  only in characteristic zero).
-/

public section

open LieAlgebra

namespace TauCeti

namespace KacMoody

/-- The generators of the free Lie algebra presenting the Kac–Moody algebra: one Cartan generator
for each element of the realization `H`, and a raising and a lowering generator for each node. -/
inductive Generator (I H : Type*)
  /-- The Cartan generator attached to an element of the realization. -/
  | cartan : H → Generator I H
  /-- The raising generator `eᵢ`. -/
  | positive : I → Generator I H
  /-- The lowering generator `fᵢ`. -/
  | negative : I → Generator I H

/-- The range of a map out of `TauCeti.KacMoody.Generator I H` splits into the union of the ranges
of its restrictions to the Cartan, raising, and lowering constructors. -/
theorem range_generator {I H α : Type*} (f : Generator I H → α) :
    Set.range f = Set.range (fun x => f (.cartan x)) ∪
      Set.range (fun i => f (.positive i)) ∪ Set.range (fun i => f (.negative i)) := by
  ext y
  simp only [Set.mem_union, Set.mem_range]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨x | i | i, rfl⟩
    · exact Or.inl (Or.inl ⟨x, rfl⟩)
    · exact Or.inl (Or.inr ⟨i, rfl⟩)
    · exact Or.inr ⟨i, rfl⟩
  · rintro ((⟨x, rfl⟩ | ⟨i, rfl⟩) | ⟨i, rfl⟩)
    · exact ⟨.cartan x, rfl⟩
    · exact ⟨.positive i, rfl⟩
    · exact ⟨.negative i, rfl⟩

variable {I K H : Type*} [Field K] [AddCommGroup H] [Module K H] {A : Matrix I I ℤ}
  (R : CartanRealization (A.map (Int.cast : ℤ → K)) H)

open _root_.FreeLieAlgebra Generator in
/-- The Cartan-linearity and Chevalley relators of a realization `R` (all relators except the
Serre relations), as elements of the free Lie algebra on `TauCeti.KacMoody.Generator I H`. -/
inductive IsAuxRelator : FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) → Prop
  /-- Additivity of the Cartan generators. -/
  | cartan_add (x y : H) :
      IsAuxRelator (of K (cartan (x + y)) - of K (cartan x) - of K (cartan y))
  /-- Homogeneity of the Cartan generators. -/
  | cartan_smul (c : K) (x : H) : IsAuxRelator (of K (cartan (c • x)) - c • of K (cartan x))
  /-- The Cartan generators commute. -/
  | lie_cartan_cartan (x y : H) :
      IsAuxRelator ⁅of K (cartan x : Generator I H), of K (cartan y)⁆
  /-- `eⱼ` has weight `αⱼ`. -/
  | lie_cartan_positive (x : H) (j : I) :
      IsAuxRelator (⁅of K (cartan x : Generator I H), of K (positive j)⁆ -
        R.root j x • of K (positive j))
  /-- `fⱼ` has weight `-αⱼ`. -/
  | lie_cartan_negative (x : H) (j : I) :
      IsAuxRelator (⁅of K (cartan x : Generator I H), of K (negative j)⁆ +
        R.root j x • of K (negative j))
  /-- `⁅eᵢ, fᵢ⁆ = hᵢ`. -/
  | lie_positive_negative_self (i : I) :
      IsAuxRelator (⁅of K (positive i : Generator I H), of K (negative i)⁆ -
        of K (cartan (R.coroot i)))
  /-- `⁅eᵢ, fⱼ⁆ = 0` for `i ≠ j`. -/
  | lie_positive_negative_of_ne (i j : I) (hij : i ≠ j) :
      IsAuxRelator ⁅of K (positive i : Generator I H), of K (negative j)⁆

open _root_.FreeLieAlgebra Generator in
/-- The defining relators of the Kac–Moody algebra of a realization `R`, as elements of the free
Lie algebra on `TauCeti.KacMoody.Generator I H`: the Cartan-linearity and Chevalley relators
(`TauCeti.KacMoody.IsAuxRelator`) together with Serre's relations. -/
inductive IsRelator : FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) → Prop
  /-- A Cartan-linearity or Chevalley relator. -/
  | aux {x : FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H)} : IsAuxRelator R x → IsRelator x
  /-- Serre's relation on the raising generators. -/
  | serre_positive (i j : I) :
      IsRelator ((ad K _ (of K (positive i : Generator I H)) ^ (-A i j).toNat)
        ⁅of K (positive i : Generator I H), of K (positive j)⁆)
  /-- Serre's relation on the lowering generators. -/
  | serre_negative (i j : I) :
      IsRelator ((ad K _ (of K (negative i : Generator I H)) ^ (-A i j).toNat)
        ⁅of K (negative i : Generator I H), of K (negative j)⁆)

/-- The Lie ideal of the free Lie algebra generated by the auxiliary (Cartan-linearity and
Chevalley) relators. -/
noncomputable def auxIdeal : LieIdeal K (FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H)) :=
  LieSubmodule.lieSpan K _ {x | IsAuxRelator R x}

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.auxIdeal` is the Lie ideal generated by `TauCeti.KacMoody.IsAuxRelator`. -/
theorem auxIdeal_def :
    auxIdeal R = LieSubmodule.lieSpan K _ {x | IsAuxRelator R x} :=
  (rfl)

/-- The Lie ideal of the free Lie algebra generated by the defining relators. -/
noncomputable def presentationIdeal : LieIdeal K (FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H)) :=
  LieSubmodule.lieSpan K _ {x | IsRelator R x}

/-- Every auxiliary relator is a defining relator, so `auxIdeal R ≤ presentationIdeal R`. -/
theorem auxIdeal_le_presentationIdeal : auxIdeal R ≤ presentationIdeal R :=
  LieSubmodule.lieSpan_mono fun _ => IsRelator.aux

/-- The Kac–Moody algebra of the realization `R`, presented by generators and relations. -/
def PresentedLieAlgebra : Type _ :=
  FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ presentationIdeal R

noncomputable instance : LieRing (PresentedLieAlgebra R) :=
  inferInstanceAs (LieRing (FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ presentationIdeal R))

noncomputable instance : LieAlgebra K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) :=
  inferInstanceAs (LieAlgebra K (FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ presentationIdeal R))

/-! ## The generators and their relations -/

/-- The quotient map presenting `TauCeti.KacMoody.PresentedLieAlgebra R`. -/
noncomputable def presentationMk :
    FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) →ₗ⁅K⁆ PresentedLieAlgebra R :=
  LieIdeal.mkQ (presentationIdeal R)

/-- The kernel of the presentation map is the ideal generated by the relators. -/
@[simp]
theorem ker_presentationMk : (presentationMk R).ker = presentationIdeal R :=
  LieIdeal.mkQ_ker _

/-- Every element of the presented algebra is the class of an element of the free Lie algebra. -/
theorem presentationMk_surjective : Function.Surjective (presentationMk R) :=
  (presentationIdeal R).surjective_mkQ

/-- A defining relator vanishes in the presented algebra. -/
theorem presentationMk_eq_zero_of_isRelator {x : FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H)}
    (hx : IsRelator R x) :
    presentationMk R x = 0 :=
  (LieIdeal.mkQ_apply _ x).trans
    (LieSubmodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero'.mpr (LieSubmodule.subset_lieSpan hx))

/-- A linear map `φ : H → L` and families `E`, `F` of elements of a Lie algebra `L` *satisfy the
auxiliary relations* of the realization `R` when they satisfy the Cartan-linearity and Chevalley
relations (all defining relations except Serre's relations). -/
structure SatisfiesAuxRelations {L : Type*} [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L]
    (φ : H →ₗ[K] L) (E F : I → L) : Prop where
  /-- The image of `H` is abelian. -/
  lie_cartan_cartan : ∀ x y, ⁅φ x, φ y⁆ = 0
  /-- `E j` has weight `αⱼ`. -/
  lie_cartan_positive : ∀ x j, ⁅φ x, E j⁆ = R.root j x • E j
  /-- `F j` has weight `-αⱼ`. -/
  lie_cartan_negative : ∀ x j, ⁅φ x, F j⁆ = -(R.root j x • F j)
  /-- `⁅E i, F i⁆` is the image of the simple coroot `hᵢ`. -/
  lie_positive_negative_self : ∀ i, ⁅E i, F i⁆ = φ (R.coroot i)
  /-- `E i` and `F j` commute for `i ≠ j`. -/
  lie_positive_negative_of_ne : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → ⁅E i, F j⁆ = 0

/-- The values on the free generators of the homomorphism induced by relation-satisfying data. -/
def generatorMap {L : Type*} [AddCommMonoid L] [Module K L] (φ : H →ₗ[K] L) (E F : I → L) :
    Generator I H → L
  | .cartan x => φ x
  | .positive i => E i
  | .negative i => F i

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.generatorMap` sends a Cartan generator to `φ x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem generatorMap_cartan {L : Type*} [AddCommMonoid L] [Module K L]
    {φ : H →ₗ[K] L} {E F : I → L} (x : H) :
    generatorMap φ E F (.cartan x) = φ x := by rfl

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.generatorMap` sends a raising generator to `E i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem generatorMap_positive {L : Type*} [AddCommMonoid L] [Module K L]
    {φ : H →ₗ[K] L} {E F : I → L} (i : I) :
    generatorMap φ E F (.positive i) = E i := by rfl

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.generatorMap` sends a lowering generator to `F i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem generatorMap_negative {L : Type*} [AddCommMonoid L] [Module K L]
    {φ : H →ₗ[K] L} {E F : I → L} (i : I) :
    generatorMap φ E F (.negative i) = F i := by rfl

section QuotientIdeal

variable {J : LieIdeal K (FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H))}

/-- An auxiliary relator vanishes in any quotient by an ideal containing `auxIdeal R`. -/
theorem mkQ_eq_zero_of_isAuxRelator (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J)
    {x : FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H)} (hx : IsAuxRelator R x) : J.mkQ x = 0 :=
  (LieIdeal.mkQ_eq_zero J).mpr (hJ (LieSubmodule.subset_lieSpan hx))

/-- The canonical linear map from `H` into any quotient of the free Lie algebra by an ideal
containing the auxiliary relators. -/
noncomputable def quotientCartanElement (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J) :
    H →ₗ[K] FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ J where
  toFun x := J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.cartan x))
  map_add' x y := by
    have h := mkQ_eq_zero_of_isAuxRelator R hJ (.cartan_add x y)
    rwa [map_sub, map_sub, sub_sub, sub_eq_zero] at h
  map_smul' c x := by
    have h := mkQ_eq_zero_of_isAuxRelator R hJ (.cartan_smul c x)
    rwa [map_sub, map_smul, sub_eq_zero] at h

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.quotientCartanElement` sends `x` to the quotient class of the Cartan
generator. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientCartanElement_apply (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J) (x : H) :
    quotientCartanElement R hJ x = J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.cartan x)) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The generator classes in any quotient by an ideal containing `auxIdeal R` satisfy the
auxiliary relations. -/
theorem satisfiesAuxRelations_quotient (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J) :
    SatisfiesAuxRelations R (quotientCartanElement R hJ)
      (fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i)))
      (fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i))) where
  lie_cartan_cartan x y := by
    simpa [quotientCartanElement] using
      mkQ_eq_zero_of_isAuxRelator R hJ (.lie_cartan_cartan x y)
  lie_cartan_positive x j := by
    simpa [quotientCartanElement, sub_eq_zero] using
      mkQ_eq_zero_of_isAuxRelator R hJ (.lie_cartan_positive x j)
  lie_cartan_negative x j := by
    simpa [quotientCartanElement, add_eq_zero_iff_eq_neg] using
      mkQ_eq_zero_of_isAuxRelator R hJ (.lie_cartan_negative x j)
  lie_positive_negative_self i := by
    simpa [quotientCartanElement, sub_eq_zero] using
      mkQ_eq_zero_of_isAuxRelator R hJ (.lie_positive_negative_self i)
  lie_positive_negative_of_ne i j hij := by
    simpa using mkQ_eq_zero_of_isAuxRelator R hJ (.lie_positive_negative_of_ne i j hij)

/-- The Cartan elements commute in any quotient by an ideal containing `auxIdeal R`. -/
theorem lie_quotientCartanElement_quotientCartanElement (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J) (x y : H) :
    ⁅quotientCartanElement R hJ x, quotientCartanElement R hJ y⁆ = 0 :=
  (satisfiesAuxRelations_quotient R hJ).lie_cartan_cartan x y

/-- The raising generator class `eⱼ` has weight `αⱼ` in any quotient by an ideal containing
`auxIdeal R`. -/
theorem lie_quotientCartanElement_mk_positive (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J) (x : H) (j : I) :
    ⁅quotientCartanElement R hJ x, J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive j))⁆ =
      R.root j x • J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive j)) :=
  (satisfiesAuxRelations_quotient R hJ).lie_cartan_positive x j

/-- The bracket of `eⱼ` with a Cartan element in any quotient by an ideal containing
`auxIdeal R`. -/
theorem lie_mk_positive_quotientCartanElement (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J) (j : I) (x : H) :
    ⁅J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive j)), quotientCartanElement R hJ x⁆ =
      -(R.root j x • J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive j))) := by
  rw [← lie_skew, lie_quotientCartanElement_mk_positive]

/-- The lowering generator class `fⱼ` has weight `-αⱼ` in any quotient by an ideal containing
`auxIdeal R`. -/
theorem lie_quotientCartanElement_mk_negative (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J) (x : H) (j : I) :
    ⁅quotientCartanElement R hJ x, J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative j))⁆ =
      -(R.root j x • J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative j))) :=
  (satisfiesAuxRelations_quotient R hJ).lie_cartan_negative x j

/-- The bracket of `eᵢ` and `fᵢ` is the simple coroot `hᵢ` in any quotient by an ideal containing
`auxIdeal R`. -/
theorem lie_mk_positive_mk_negative_self (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J) (i : I) :
    ⁅J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i)),
        J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i))⁆ =
      quotientCartanElement R hJ (R.coroot i) :=
  (satisfiesAuxRelations_quotient R hJ).lie_positive_negative_self i

/-- The bracket of `fᵢ` and `eᵢ` is `-hᵢ` in any quotient by an ideal containing
`auxIdeal R`. -/
theorem lie_mk_negative_mk_positive_self (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J) (i : I) :
    ⁅J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)),
        J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i))⁆ =
      -quotientCartanElement R hJ (R.coroot i) := by
  rw [← lie_skew, lie_mk_positive_mk_negative_self]

/-- The generator classes `eᵢ` and `fⱼ` commute for `i ≠ j` in any quotient by an ideal
containing `auxIdeal R`. -/
theorem lie_mk_positive_mk_negative_of_ne (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J) {i j : I} (hij : i ≠ j) :
    ⁅J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i)),
        J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative j))⁆ = 0 :=
  (satisfiesAuxRelations_quotient R hJ).lie_positive_negative_of_ne i j hij

/-- The generator classes `fᵢ` and `eⱼ` commute for `i ≠ j` in any quotient by an ideal
containing `auxIdeal R`. -/
theorem lie_mk_negative_mk_positive_of_ne (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J) {i j : I} (hij : i ≠ j) :
    ⁅J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)),
        J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive j))⁆ = 0 := by
  rw [← lie_skew, lie_mk_positive_mk_negative_of_ne R hJ hij.symm, neg_zero]

section Universal

variable {R} {L : Type*} [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L]

variable (R) in
/-- Two homomorphisms out of `FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ J` agreeing on the generator
classes are equal. -/
theorem quotient_hom_ext (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J)
    {g₁ g₂ : FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ J →ₗ⁅K⁆ L}
    (hH : ∀ x, g₁ (quotientCartanElement R hJ x) = g₂ (quotientCartanElement R hJ x))
    (hE : ∀ i, g₁ (J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i))) =
      g₂ (J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i))))
    (hF : ∀ i, g₁ (J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i))) =
      g₂ (J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)))) : g₁ = g₂ :=
  TauCeti.FreeLieAlgebra.quotient_hom_ext fun
    | .cartan x => hH x
    | .positive i => hE i
    | .negative i => hF i

end Universal

/-- The Chevalley involution on any quotient of `FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H)` by a Lie ideal
`J ≥ auxIdeal R` stable under negating the Cartan generators and swapping `eᵢ` with `-fᵢ`. -/
noncomputable def quotientChevalleyInvolution (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J)
    (hker : J ≤ (FreeLieAlgebra.lift K (generatorMap (-quotientCartanElement R hJ)
      (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)))
      (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i))))).ker) :
    (FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ J) ≃ₗ⁅K⁆ (FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ J) :=
  let f := J.liftQ (FreeLieAlgebra.lift K (generatorMap (-quotientCartanElement R hJ)
    (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)))
    (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i))))) hker
  have hf : f.comp f = LieHom.id :=
    quotient_hom_ext R hJ
      (fun x => by simp [f])
      (fun i => by simp [f])
      (fun i => by simp [f])
  { toLieHom := f
    invFun := f
    left_inv := DFunLike.congr_fun hf
    right_inv := DFunLike.congr_fun hf }

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.quotientChevalleyInvolution` negates Cartan generator classes. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientChevalleyInvolution_mk_cartan (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J)
    (hker : J ≤ (FreeLieAlgebra.lift K (generatorMap (-quotientCartanElement R hJ)
      (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)))
      (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i))))).ker)
    (x : H) :
    quotientChevalleyInvolution R hJ hker
        (LieSubmodule.Quotient.mk (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.cartan x)) :
          FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ J) =
      -(LieSubmodule.Quotient.mk (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.cartan x)) :
        FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ J) := by
  simp [quotientChevalleyInvolution]

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.quotientChevalleyInvolution` sends `eᵢ` to `-fᵢ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientChevalleyInvolution_mk_positive (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J)
    (hker : J ≤ (FreeLieAlgebra.lift K (generatorMap (-quotientCartanElement R hJ)
      (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)))
      (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i))))).ker)
    (i : I) :
    quotientChevalleyInvolution R hJ hker
        (LieSubmodule.Quotient.mk (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i)) :
          FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ J) =
      -(LieSubmodule.Quotient.mk (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)) :
        FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ J) := by
  simp [quotientChevalleyInvolution]

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.quotientChevalleyInvolution` sends `fᵢ` to `-eᵢ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientChevalleyInvolution_mk_negative (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J)
    (hker : J ≤ (FreeLieAlgebra.lift K (generatorMap (-quotientCartanElement R hJ)
      (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)))
      (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i))))).ker)
    (i : I) :
    quotientChevalleyInvolution R hJ hker
        (LieSubmodule.Quotient.mk (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)) :
          FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ J) =
      -(LieSubmodule.Quotient.mk (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i)) :
        FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ J) := by
  simp [quotientChevalleyInvolution]

/-- Applying `TauCeti.KacMoody.quotientChevalleyInvolution` twice is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientChevalleyInvolution_apply_apply (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J)
    (hker : J ≤ (FreeLieAlgebra.lift K (generatorMap (-quotientCartanElement R hJ)
      (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)))
      (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i))))).ker)
    (y : FreeLieAlgebra K (Generator I H) ⧸ J) :
    quotientChevalleyInvolution R hJ hker (quotientChevalleyInvolution R hJ hker y) = y :=
  (quotientChevalleyInvolution R hJ hker).left_inv y

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.quotientChevalleyInvolution` is its own inverse. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientChevalleyInvolution_symm (hJ : auxIdeal R ≤ J)
    (hker : J ≤ (FreeLieAlgebra.lift K (generatorMap (-quotientCartanElement R hJ)
      (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)))
      (-fun i => J.mkQ (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i))))).ker) :
    (quotientChevalleyInvolution R hJ hker).symm = quotientChevalleyInvolution R hJ hker :=
  LieEquiv.ext fun y =>
    (LieEquiv.symm_apply_eq _).2 (quotientChevalleyInvolution_apply_apply R hJ hker y).symm

end QuotientIdeal

/-- The canonical linear map from the realization `H` into the presented algebra, sending `h` to
the class of its Cartan generator. No injectivity is claimed for it here. -/
noncomputable def cartanElement : H →ₗ[K] PresentedLieAlgebra R :=
  quotientCartanElement R (auxIdeal_le_presentationIdeal R)

/-- The raising generator `eᵢ` of the presented algebra. -/
noncomputable def positiveGenerator (i : I) : PresentedLieAlgebra R :=
  presentationMk R (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i))

/-- The lowering generator `fᵢ` of the presented algebra. -/
noncomputable def negativeGenerator (i : I) : PresentedLieAlgebra R :=
  presentationMk R (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i))

/-- The quotient map sends the free Cartan generator of `x` to `TauCeti.KacMoody.cartanElement`. -/
@[simp]
theorem presentationMk_of_cartan (x : H) :
    presentationMk R (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.cartan x)) = cartanElement R x := (rfl)

/-- The quotient map sends the free generator `eᵢ` to `TauCeti.KacMoody.positiveGenerator`. -/
@[simp]
theorem presentationMk_of_positive (i : I) :
    presentationMk R (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.positive i)) = positiveGenerator R i := (rfl)

/-- The quotient map sends the free generator `fᵢ` to `TauCeti.KacMoody.negativeGenerator`. -/
@[simp]
theorem presentationMk_of_negative (i : I) :
    presentationMk R (FreeLieAlgebra.of K (Generator.negative i)) = negativeGenerator R i := (rfl)

/-- The raising subalgebra `n⁺` of `PresentedLieAlgebra R`, generated by the `eᵢ`. -/
noncomputable def positiveSubalgebra : LieSubalgebra K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) :=
  LieSubalgebra.lieSpan K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) (Set.range (positiveGenerator R))

/-- The defining `lieSpan` description of `TauCeti.KacMoody.positiveSubalgebra`. -/
theorem positiveSubalgebra_def :
    positiveSubalgebra R =
      LieSubalgebra.lieSpan K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) (Set.range (positiveGenerator R)) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The lowering subalgebra `n⁻` of `PresentedLieAlgebra R`, generated by the `fᵢ`. -/
noncomputable def negativeSubalgebra : LieSubalgebra K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) :=
  LieSubalgebra.lieSpan K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) (Set.range (negativeGenerator R))

/-- The defining `lieSpan` description of `TauCeti.KacMoody.negativeSubalgebra`. -/
theorem negativeSubalgebra_def :
    negativeSubalgebra R =
      LieSubalgebra.lieSpan K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) (Set.range (negativeGenerator R)) :=
  (rfl)

/-- Each raising generator `eᵢ` belongs to `TauCeti.KacMoody.positiveSubalgebra`. -/
@[simp]
theorem positiveGenerator_mem_positiveSubalgebra (i : I) :
    positiveGenerator R i ∈ positiveSubalgebra R :=
  LieSubalgebra.subset_lieSpan (Set.mem_range_self i)

/-- Each lowering generator `fᵢ` belongs to `TauCeti.KacMoody.negativeSubalgebra`. -/
@[simp]
theorem negativeGenerator_mem_negativeSubalgebra (i : I) :
    negativeGenerator R i ∈ negativeSubalgebra R :=
  LieSubalgebra.subset_lieSpan (Set.mem_range_self i)

/-- The Cartan elements commute. -/
@[simp]
theorem lie_cartanElement_cartanElement (x y : H) :
    ⁅cartanElement R x, cartanElement R y⁆ = 0 :=
  lie_quotientCartanElement_quotientCartanElement R (auxIdeal_le_presentationIdeal R) x y

/-- The raising generator `eⱼ` has weight `αⱼ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lie_cartanElement_positiveGenerator (x : H) (j : I) :
    ⁅cartanElement R x, positiveGenerator R j⁆ = R.root j x • positiveGenerator R j :=
  lie_quotientCartanElement_mk_positive R (auxIdeal_le_presentationIdeal R) x j

/-- The lowering generator `fⱼ` has weight `-αⱼ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lie_cartanElement_negativeGenerator (x : H) (j : I) :
    ⁅cartanElement R x, negativeGenerator R j⁆ = -(R.root j x • negativeGenerator R j) :=
  lie_quotientCartanElement_mk_negative R (auxIdeal_le_presentationIdeal R) x j

/-- The bracket of `eᵢ` and `fᵢ` is the simple coroot `hᵢ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lie_positiveGenerator_negativeGenerator_self (i : I) :
    ⁅positiveGenerator R i, negativeGenerator R i⁆ = cartanElement R (R.coroot i) :=
  lie_mk_positive_mk_negative_self R (auxIdeal_le_presentationIdeal R) i

/-- The generators `eᵢ` and `fⱼ` commute for `i ≠ j`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lie_positiveGenerator_negativeGenerator_of_ne {i j : I} (hij : i ≠ j) :
    ⁅positiveGenerator R i, negativeGenerator R j⁆ = 0 :=
  lie_mk_positive_mk_negative_of_ne R (auxIdeal_le_presentationIdeal R) hij

/-- Serre's relation `(ad eᵢ) ^ (-Aᵢⱼ) ⁅eᵢ, eⱼ⁆ = 0` on the raising generators. -/
@[simp]
theorem ad_pow_lie_positiveGenerator_positiveGenerator (i j : I) :
    (ad K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) (positiveGenerator R i) ^ (-A i j).toNat)
      ⁅positiveGenerator R i, positiveGenerator R j⁆ = 0 := by
  have h := presentationMk_eq_zero_of_isRelator R (.serre_positive i j)
  rwa [LieHom.map_ad_pow, LieHom.map_lie] at h

/-- Serre's relation `(ad fᵢ) ^ (-Aᵢⱼ) ⁅fᵢ, fⱼ⁆ = 0` on the lowering generators. -/
@[simp]
theorem ad_pow_lie_negativeGenerator_negativeGenerator (i j : I) :
    (ad K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) (negativeGenerator R i) ^ (-A i j).toNat)
      ⁅negativeGenerator R i, negativeGenerator R j⁆ = 0 := by
  have h := presentationMk_eq_zero_of_isRelator R (.serre_negative i j)
  rwa [LieHom.map_ad_pow, LieHom.map_lie] at h

/-! ## The universal property -/

variable {L : Type*} [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L]

/-- A linear map `φ : H → L` and families `E`, `F` of elements of a Lie algebra `L` *satisfy the
relations* of the Kac–Moody algebra of `R` when they satisfy the auxiliary relations
(`TauCeti.KacMoody.SatisfiesAuxRelations`) together with Serre's relations. -/
structure SatisfiesRelations (φ : H →ₗ[K] L) (E F : I → L) : Prop
    extends SatisfiesAuxRelations R φ E F where
  /-- Serre's relation on the raising family. -/
  serre_positive : ∀ i j, (ad K L (E i) ^ (-A i j).toNat) ⁅E i, E j⁆ = 0
  /-- Serre's relation on the lowering family. -/
  serre_negative : ∀ i j, (ad K L (F i) ^ (-A i j).toNat) ⁅F i, F j⁆ = 0

/-- The generators of the presented algebra satisfy its relations. -/
theorem satisfiesRelations_generators :
    SatisfiesRelations R (cartanElement R) (positiveGenerator R) (negativeGenerator R) where
  lie_cartan_cartan := lie_cartanElement_cartanElement R
  lie_cartan_positive := lie_cartanElement_positiveGenerator R
  lie_cartan_negative := lie_cartanElement_negativeGenerator R
  lie_positive_negative_self := lie_positiveGenerator_negativeGenerator_self R
  lie_positive_negative_of_ne _ _ := lie_positiveGenerator_negativeGenerator_of_ne R
  serre_positive := ad_pow_lie_positiveGenerator_positiveGenerator R
  serre_negative := ad_pow_lie_negativeGenerator_negativeGenerator R

variable {R}

/-- Auxiliary relations are carried along Lie algebra homomorphisms. -/
theorem SatisfiesAuxRelations.map {φ : H →ₗ[K] L} {E F : I → L}
    (h : SatisfiesAuxRelations R φ E F) {L' : Type*} [LieRing L'] [LieAlgebra K L']
    (g : L →ₗ⁅K⁆ L') :
    SatisfiesAuxRelations R ((g : L →ₗ[K] L') ∘ₗ φ) (g ∘ E) (g ∘ F) where
  lie_cartan_cartan x y := by simp [← LieHom.map_lie, h.lie_cartan_cartan]
  lie_cartan_positive x j := by simp [← LieHom.map_lie, h.lie_cartan_positive]
  lie_cartan_negative x j := by simp [← LieHom.map_lie, h.lie_cartan_negative]
  lie_positive_negative_self i := by simp [← LieHom.map_lie, h.lie_positive_negative_self]
  lie_positive_negative_of_ne i j hij := by
    simp [← LieHom.map_lie, h.lie_positive_negative_of_ne i j hij]

/-- Negating the Cartan map and exchanging the raising and lowering families with a minus sign
preserves the Cartan-linearity and Chevalley relations. -/
theorem SatisfiesAuxRelations.neg_swap {φ : H →ₗ[K] L} {E F : I → L}
    (h : SatisfiesAuxRelations R φ E F) :
    SatisfiesAuxRelations R (-φ) (-F) (-E) where
  lie_cartan_cartan x y := by simp [h.lie_cartan_cartan]
  lie_cartan_positive x j := by simp [h.lie_cartan_negative]
  lie_cartan_negative x j := by simp [h.lie_cartan_positive]
  lie_positive_negative_self i := by
    simp [← lie_skew (F i) (E i), h.lie_positive_negative_self]
  lie_positive_negative_of_ne i j hij := by
    simp [← lie_skew (F i) (E j), h.lie_positive_negative_of_ne j i hij.symm]

/-- Relations are carried along Lie algebra homomorphisms. -/
theorem SatisfiesRelations.map {φ : H →ₗ[K] L} {E F : I → L} (h : SatisfiesRelations R φ E F)
    {L' : Type*} [LieRing L'] [LieAlgebra K L'] (g : L →ₗ⁅K⁆ L') :
    SatisfiesRelations R ((g : L →ₗ[K] L') ∘ₗ φ) (g ∘ E) (g ∘ F) :=
  { h.toSatisfiesAuxRelations.map g with
    serre_positive := fun i j => by
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, ← LieHom.map_lie, ← LieHom.map_ad_pow, h.serre_positive,
        map_zero]
    serre_negative := fun i j => by
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, ← LieHom.map_lie, ← LieHom.map_ad_pow, h.serre_negative,
        map_zero] }

/-- Negating the Cartan map and exchanging the raising and lowering families with a minus sign
preserves the defining relations of the Kac–Moody algebra. -/
theorem SatisfiesRelations.neg_swap {φ : H →ₗ[K] L} {E F : I → L}
    (h : SatisfiesRelations R φ E F) :
    SatisfiesRelations R (-φ) (-F) (-E) :=
  { h.toSatisfiesAuxRelations.neg_swap with
    serre_positive := fun i j => by
      simpa using ad_neg_pow_apply_eq_zero (x := F i) (n := (-A i j).toNat) (y := ⁅F i, F j⁆)
        (h.serre_negative i j)
    serre_negative := fun i j => by
      simpa using ad_neg_pow_apply_eq_zero (x := E i) (n := (-A i j).toNat) (y := ⁅E i, E j⁆)
        (h.serre_positive i j) }

/-- The zero map satisfies the relations. -/
theorem satisfiesRelations_zero : SatisfiesRelations R (0 : H →ₗ[K] L) 0 0 where
  lie_cartan_cartan _ _ := by simp
  lie_cartan_positive _ _ := by simp
  lie_cartan_negative _ _ := by simp
  lie_positive_negative_self _ := by simp
  lie_positive_negative_of_ne _ _ _ := by simp
  serre_positive _ _ := by simp
  serre_negative _ _ := by simp

variable {φ : H →ₗ[K] L} {E F : I → L}

/-- Auxiliary-relation-satisfying data kill every auxiliary relator. -/
theorem auxIdeal_le_ker (h : SatisfiesAuxRelations R φ E F) :
    auxIdeal R ≤ (FreeLieAlgebra.lift K (generatorMap φ E F)).ker := by
  rw [auxIdeal_def]
  refine LieSubmodule.lieSpan_le.mpr fun x hx => ?_
  rw [SetLike.mem_coe, LieHom.mem_ker]
  induction hx with
  | cartan_add x y => simp [generatorMap]
  | cartan_smul c x => simp [generatorMap]
  | lie_cartan_cartan x y => simpa [generatorMap] using h.lie_cartan_cartan x y
  | lie_cartan_positive x j => simpa [generatorMap, sub_eq_zero] using h.lie_cartan_positive x j
  | lie_cartan_negative x j =>
    simpa [generatorMap, add_eq_zero_iff_eq_neg] using h.lie_cartan_negative x j
  | lie_positive_negative_self i =>
    simpa [generatorMap, sub_eq_zero] using h.lie_positive_negative_self i
  | lie_positive_negative_of_ne i j hij =>
    simpa [generatorMap] using h.lie_positive_negative_of_ne i j hij

/-- Relation-satisfying data kill every relator. -/
theorem presentationIdeal_le_ker (h : SatisfiesRelations R φ E F) :
    presentationIdeal R ≤ (FreeLieAlgebra.lift K (generatorMap φ E F)).ker := by
  refine LieSubmodule.lieSpan_le.mpr fun x hx => ?_
  rcases hx with ⟨hx⟩ | ⟨i, j⟩ | ⟨i, j⟩
  · exact auxIdeal_le_ker h.toSatisfiesAuxRelations (LieSubmodule.subset_lieSpan hx)
  · rw [SetLike.mem_coe, LieHom.mem_ker]
    simpa [LieHom.map_ad_pow, generatorMap] using h.serre_positive i j
  · rw [SetLike.mem_coe, LieHom.mem_ker]
    simpa [LieHom.map_ad_pow, generatorMap] using h.serre_negative i j

/-- The homomorphism out of the presented algebra determined by data satisfying its relations:
the universal property of the presentation. -/
noncomputable def lift (h : SatisfiesRelations R φ E F) : PresentedLieAlgebra R →ₗ⁅K⁆ L :=
  (presentationIdeal R).liftQ (FreeLieAlgebra.lift K (generatorMap φ E F))
    (presentationIdeal_le_ker h)

/-- The lift sends the Cartan elements along `φ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_cartanElement (h : SatisfiesRelations R φ E F) (x : H) :
    lift h (cartanElement R x) = φ x :=
  (LieIdeal.liftQ_apply _ _ _ _).trans (FreeLieAlgebra.lift_of_apply _ _)

/-- The lift sends `eᵢ` to `E i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_positiveGenerator (h : SatisfiesRelations R φ E F) (i : I) :
    lift h (positiveGenerator R i) = E i :=
  (LieIdeal.liftQ_apply _ _ _ _).trans (FreeLieAlgebra.lift_of_apply _ _)

/-- The lift sends `fᵢ` to `F i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_negativeGenerator (h : SatisfiesRelations R φ E F) (i : I) :
    lift h (negativeGenerator R i) = F i :=
  (LieIdeal.liftQ_apply _ _ _ _).trans (FreeLieAlgebra.lift_of_apply _ _)

/-- Two homomorphisms out of the presented algebra agreeing on the generators are equal. -/
@[ext]
theorem hom_ext {g₁ g₂ : PresentedLieAlgebra R →ₗ⁅K⁆ L}
    (hH : ∀ x, g₁ (cartanElement R x) = g₂ (cartanElement R x))
    (hE : ∀ i, g₁ (positiveGenerator R i) = g₂ (positiveGenerator R i))
    (hF : ∀ i, g₁ (negativeGenerator R i) = g₂ (negativeGenerator R i)) : g₁ = g₂ :=
  quotient_hom_ext R (auxIdeal_le_presentationIdeal R) hH hE hF

/-- Two Lie equivalences out of `TauCeti.KacMoody.PresentedLieAlgebra R` agreeing on the
generators are equal. -/
@[ext]
theorem equiv_ext {e₁ e₂ : PresentedLieAlgebra R ≃ₗ⁅K⁆ L}
    (hH : ∀ x, e₁ (cartanElement R x) = e₂ (cartanElement R x))
    (hE : ∀ i, e₁ (positiveGenerator R i) = e₂ (positiveGenerator R i))
    (hF : ∀ i, e₁ (negativeGenerator R i) = e₂ (negativeGenerator R i)) : e₁ = e₂ :=
  LieEquiv.ext fun x => DFunLike.congr_fun (hom_ext hH hE hF) x

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.lift` is the unique homomorphism with the prescribed values on the
generators. -/
theorem eq_lift {h : SatisfiesRelations R φ E F} {g : PresentedLieAlgebra R →ₗ⁅K⁆ L}
    (hH : ∀ x, g (cartanElement R x) = φ x) (hE : ∀ i, g (positiveGenerator R i) = E i)
    (hF : ∀ i, g (negativeGenerator R i) = F i) : g = lift h :=
  hom_ext (by simpa using hH) (by simpa using hE) (by simpa using hF)

variable (R)

/-- Every homomorphism out of the presented algebra is the lift of the images of the
generators. -/
theorem lift_map_satisfiesRelations_generators (g : PresentedLieAlgebra R →ₗ⁅K⁆ L) :
    lift ((satisfiesRelations_generators R).map g) = g :=
  (eq_lift (fun _ => rfl) (fun _ => rfl) fun _ => rfl).symm

/-- Composing a lift with a homomorphism lifts the composed data. -/
theorem comp_lift (h : SatisfiesRelations R φ E F) {L' : Type*} [LieRing L'] [LieAlgebra K L']
    (g : L →ₗ⁅K⁆ L') : g.comp (lift h) = lift (h.map g) := by
  ext <;> simp

/-- Lifting the generators of the presented algebra along themselves gives the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_generators : lift (satisfiesRelations_generators R) = LieHom.id := by
  ext <;> simp

/-- Lifting the zero data gives the zero homomorphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_zero : lift (satisfiesRelations_zero (R := R) (L := L)) = 0 := by
  ext <;> simp

/-- The **Chevalley involution** of `TauCeti.KacMoody.PresentedLieAlgebra R`: the Lie algebra
automorphism acting as `-1` on `H` and exchanging `eᵢ` with `-fᵢ`. -/
noncomputable def chevalleyInvolution : PresentedLieAlgebra R ≃ₗ⁅K⁆ PresentedLieAlgebra R :=
  quotientChevalleyInvolution R (auxIdeal_le_presentationIdeal R)
    (presentationIdeal_le_ker (satisfiesRelations_generators R).neg_swap)

/-- The Chevalley involution negates Cartan elements. -/
@[simp]
theorem chevalleyInvolution_cartanElement (x : H) :
    chevalleyInvolution R (cartanElement R x) = -cartanElement R x :=
  quotientChevalleyInvolution_mk_cartan R _ _ x

/-- The Chevalley involution sends `eᵢ` to `-fᵢ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem chevalleyInvolution_positiveGenerator (i : I) :
    chevalleyInvolution R (positiveGenerator R i) = -negativeGenerator R i :=
  quotientChevalleyInvolution_mk_positive R _ _ i

/-- The Chevalley involution sends `fᵢ` to `-eᵢ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem chevalleyInvolution_negativeGenerator (i : I) :
    chevalleyInvolution R (negativeGenerator R i) = -positiveGenerator R i :=
  quotientChevalleyInvolution_mk_negative R _ _ i

variable {R} in
/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.chevalleyInvolution` is the unique Lie endomorphism negating `H` and
exchanging `eᵢ` with `-fᵢ`. -/
theorem eq_chevalleyInvolution {g : PresentedLieAlgebra R →ₗ⁅K⁆ PresentedLieAlgebra R}
    (hH : ∀ x, g (cartanElement R x) = -cartanElement R x)
    (hE : ∀ i, g (positiveGenerator R i) = -negativeGenerator R i)
    (hF : ∀ i, g (negativeGenerator R i) = -positiveGenerator R i) :
    g = (chevalleyInvolution R : PresentedLieAlgebra R →ₗ⁅K⁆ PresentedLieAlgebra R) :=
  hom_ext (by simpa using hH) (by simpa using hE) (by simpa using hF)

/-- Applying the Chevalley involution twice is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem chevalleyInvolution_chevalleyInvolution (x : PresentedLieAlgebra R) :
    chevalleyInvolution R (chevalleyInvolution R x) = x :=
  quotientChevalleyInvolution_apply_apply R _ _ x

/-- The Chevalley involution is involutive. -/
theorem chevalleyInvolution_involutive : Function.Involutive (chevalleyInvolution R) :=
  chevalleyInvolution_chevalleyInvolution R

/-- The Chevalley involution is its own inverse. -/
@[simp]
theorem chevalleyInvolution_symm : (chevalleyInvolution R).symm = chevalleyInvolution R :=
  quotientChevalleyInvolution_symm R _ _

/-- Naturality of the Chevalley involution with respect to `TauCeti.KacMoody.lift`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_comp_chevalleyInvolution {L : Type*} [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L]
    {φ : H →ₗ[K] L} {E F : I → L} (h : SatisfiesRelations R φ E F) :
    (lift h).comp (chevalleyInvolution R : PresentedLieAlgebra R →ₗ⁅K⁆ PresentedLieAlgebra R) =
      lift h.neg_swap := by
  ext <;> simp

/-- The Cartan elements and the raising and lowering generators generate the presented algebra
as a Lie algebra. -/
theorem lieSpan_generators_eq_top :
    LieSubalgebra.lieSpan K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) (Set.range (cartanElement R) ∪
      Set.range (positiveGenerator R) ∪ Set.range (negativeGenerator R)) = ⊤ := by
  have hrange : Set.range (fun g => presentationMk R (FreeLieAlgebra.of K g)) =
      Set.range (cartanElement R) ∪ Set.range (positiveGenerator R) ∪
        Set.range (negativeGenerator R) := by
    rw [range_generator]; rfl
  rw [← hrange]
  exact LieIdeal.lieSpan_range_mkQ_of_eq_top (presentationIdeal R)

/-- A Cartan vector annihilated by every simple root is central in the presented algebra. -/
theorem cartanElement_mem_center {z : H} (hz : z ∈ R.cartanCenter) :
    cartanElement R z ∈ center K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) := by
  have hr := (R.mem_cartanCenter_iff z).mp hz
  rw [LieModule.mem_maxTrivSubmodule]
  have h := lieSpan_le_lieAnnihilator (R := K) (L := PresentedLieAlgebra R)
    (M := PresentedLieAlgebra R)
    (s := Set.range (cartanElement R) ∪ Set.range (positiveGenerator R) ∪
      Set.range (negativeGenerator R)) (v := cartanElement R z) ?_
  · rw [lieSpan_generators_eq_top] at h
    exact fun x => (mem_lieAnnihilator K _).mp (h (LieSubalgebra.mem_top x))
  rintro _ ((⟨x, rfl⟩ | ⟨i, rfl⟩) | ⟨i, rfl⟩) <;>
    rw [← lie_skew] <;> simp [hr]

section CartanInjective

variable {R} (hinj : Function.Injective (cartanElement R))
include hinj

/-- Whenever `cartanElement R` is injective, every raising generator `eᵢ` is nonzero. -/
theorem positiveGenerator_ne_zero_of_injective (i : I) : positiveGenerator R i ≠ 0 := fun h0 =>
  R.coroot_linearIndependent.ne_zero i <| hinj <| by
    simpa [h0] using (lie_positiveGenerator_negativeGenerator_self R i).symm

/-- Whenever `cartanElement R` is injective, every lowering generator `fᵢ` is nonzero. -/
theorem negativeGenerator_ne_zero_of_injective (i : I) : negativeGenerator R i ≠ 0 := fun h0 =>
  R.coroot_linearIndependent.ne_zero i <| hinj <| by
    simpa [h0] using (lie_positiveGenerator_negativeGenerator_self R i).symm

/-- Whenever `cartanElement R` is injective, the images of the simple coroots in
`TauCeti.KacMoody.PresentedLieAlgebra R` are linearly independent. -/
theorem linearIndependent_cartanElement_coroot :
    LinearIndependent K (fun i => cartanElement R (R.coroot i)) :=
  R.coroot_linearIndependent.map' (cartanElement R) (LinearMap.ker_eq_bot.2 hinj)

/-- Whenever `cartanElement R` is injective, `cartanElement R x` lies in the center of
`TauCeti.KacMoody.PresentedLieAlgebra R` if and only if `x` lies in `R.cartanCenter`. -/
theorem cartanElement_mem_center_iff {x : H} :
    cartanElement R x ∈ center K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) ↔ x ∈ R.cartanCenter := by
  refine ⟨fun hx => (R.mem_cartanCenter_iff x).2 fun i => ?_, cartanElement_mem_center R⟩
  have h0 : ⁅cartanElement R x, positiveGenerator R i⁆ = 0 := by
    rw [← lie_skew, (LieModule.mem_maxTrivSubmodule K _ _ _).1 hx (positiveGenerator R i), neg_zero]
  rw [lie_cartanElement_positiveGenerator] at h0
  exact (smul_eq_zero.1 h0).resolve_right (positiveGenerator_ne_zero_of_injective hinj i)

end CartanInjective

/-! ## The derived algebra and Serre's presentation

Mathlib's `Matrix.ToLieAlgebra K A` presents a Lie algebra on generators `hᵢ`, `eᵢ`, `fᵢ` alone. The
relations of the full realization restrict to its relations, giving a homomorphism
`TauCeti.KacMoody.serreHom` into the presented algebra. Its image is the derived algebra, and
together with the Cartan elements it spans the whole algebra. -/

section Serre

variable {R}

/-- Data satisfying the relations of the full realization restrict to a Serre system for `A` on
the images of the simple coroots. -/
theorem SatisfiesRelations.isSerreSystem (h : SatisfiesRelations R φ E F) :
    IsSerreSystem K A (fun i => φ (R.coroot i)) E F where
  lie_H_H _ _ := h.lie_cartan_cartan _ _
  lie_E_F_self := h.lie_positive_negative_self
  lie_E_F_of_ne := h.lie_positive_negative_of_ne
  lie_H_E i j := by simp [h.lie_cartan_positive, Int.cast_smul_eq_zsmul]
  lie_H_F i j := by simp [h.lie_cartan_negative, Int.cast_smul_eq_zsmul]
  ad_pow_lie_E_E := h.serre_positive
  ad_pow_lie_F_F := h.serre_negative

section QuotientMaps

variable (R)

/-- The canonical homomorphism from `FreeLieAlgebra K I ⧸ serreIdeal K A` to
`PresentedLieAlgebra R` sending the `i`-th generator to `eᵢ`. -/
noncomputable def positiveQuotientHom :
    FreeLieAlgebra K I ⧸ serreIdeal K A →ₗ⁅K⁆ PresentedLieAlgebra R :=
  serreIdealLift (ad_pow_lie_positiveGenerator_positiveGenerator R)

/-- Composing `TauCeti.KacMoody.positiveQuotientHom` with the quotient map recovers the lift on
the free Lie algebra. -/
@[simp]
theorem positiveQuotientHom_comp_mkQ :
    (positiveQuotientHom R).comp (serreIdeal K A).mkQ =
      FreeLieAlgebra.lift K (positiveGenerator R) :=
  serreIdealLift_comp_mkQ _

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.positiveQuotientHom` sends the quotient class of the `i`-th free generator
to `eᵢ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem positiveQuotientHom_mk_of (i : I) :
    positiveQuotientHom R (LieSubmodule.Quotient.mk (FreeLieAlgebra.of K i)) =
      positiveGenerator R i :=
  serreIdealLift_mk_of _ i

/-- The range of `TauCeti.KacMoody.positiveQuotientHom` is `n⁺`. -/
theorem range_positiveQuotientHom : (positiveQuotientHom R).range = positiveSubalgebra R :=
  range_serreIdealLift _

/-- The canonical homomorphism from `FreeLieAlgebra K I ⧸ serreIdeal K A` to
`PresentedLieAlgebra R` sending the `i`-th generator to `fᵢ`. -/
noncomputable def negativeQuotientHom :
    FreeLieAlgebra K I ⧸ serreIdeal K A →ₗ⁅K⁆ PresentedLieAlgebra R :=
  serreIdealLift (ad_pow_lie_negativeGenerator_negativeGenerator R)

/-- Composing `TauCeti.KacMoody.negativeQuotientHom` with the quotient map recovers the lift on
the free Lie algebra. -/
@[simp]
theorem negativeQuotientHom_comp_mkQ :
    (negativeQuotientHom R).comp (serreIdeal K A).mkQ =
      FreeLieAlgebra.lift K (negativeGenerator R) :=
  serreIdealLift_comp_mkQ _

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.negativeQuotientHom` sends the quotient class of the `i`-th free generator
to `fᵢ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem negativeQuotientHom_mk_of (i : I) :
    negativeQuotientHom R (LieSubmodule.Quotient.mk (FreeLieAlgebra.of K i)) =
      negativeGenerator R i :=
  serreIdealLift_mk_of _ i

/-- The range of `TauCeti.KacMoody.negativeQuotientHom` is `n⁻`. -/
theorem range_negativeQuotientHom : (negativeQuotientHom R).range = negativeSubalgebra R :=
  range_serreIdealLift _

end QuotientMaps

variable [DecidableEq I] (R)

/-- The homomorphism from Serre's presentation `Matrix.ToLieAlgebra K A` to the Kac–Moody algebra
of the realization `R`, sending `hᵢ`, `eᵢ`, `fᵢ` to the simple coroot `cartanElement R hᵢ` and to
the generators `eᵢ`, `fᵢ`. -/
noncomputable def serreHom : Matrix.ToLieAlgebra K A →ₗ⁅K⁆ PresentedLieAlgebra R :=
  serreLift (satisfiesRelations_generators R).isSerreSystem

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.serreHom` sends `hᵢ` to the simple coroot. -/
@[simp]
theorem serreHom_serreH (i : I) : serreHom R (serreH K A i) = cartanElement R (R.coroot i) :=
  serreLift_serreH _ i

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.serreHom` sends `eᵢ` to `eᵢ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem serreHom_serreE (i : I) : serreHom R (serreE K A i) = positiveGenerator R i :=
  serreLift_serreE _ i

/-- `TauCeti.KacMoody.serreHom` sends `fᵢ` to `fᵢ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem serreHom_serreF (i : I) : serreHom R (serreF K A i) = negativeGenerator R i :=
  serreLift_serreF _ i

/-- The image of Serre's presentation is the Lie subalgebra generated by the `eᵢ` and `fᵢ`. -/
theorem range_serreHom : (serreHom R).range = LieSubalgebra.lieSpan K (PresentedLieAlgebra R)
    (Set.range (positiveGenerator R) ∪ Set.range (negativeGenerator R)) := by
  rw [LieHom.range_eq_map, ← lieSpan_serreE_union_serreF_eq_top K A, LieSubalgebra.map_lieSpan,
    Set.image_union, ← Set.range_comp, ← Set.range_comp]
  congr <;> funext i <;> simp

/-- Bracketing with a Cartan element preserves the image of Serre's presentation. -/
private theorem lie_cartanElement_mem_range_serreHom (x : H) {y : PresentedLieAlgebra R}
    (hy : y ∈ (serreHom R).range) : ⁅cartanElement R x, y⁆ ∈ (serreHom R).range := by
  rw [range_serreHom] at hy ⊢
  induction hy using LieSubalgebra.lieSpan_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    rcases hy with ⟨i, rfl⟩ | ⟨i, rfl⟩
    · rw [lie_cartanElement_positiveGenerator]
      exact LieSubalgebra.smul_mem _ _ (LieSubalgebra.subset_lieSpan (Or.inl ⟨i, rfl⟩))
    · rw [lie_cartanElement_negativeGenerator]
      exact neg_mem (LieSubalgebra.smul_mem _ _ (LieSubalgebra.subset_lieSpan (Or.inr ⟨i, rfl⟩)))
  | zero => simp
  | add y z _ _ hy hz => simpa only [lie_add] using add_mem hy hz
  | smul c y _ hy => simpa only [lie_smul] using LieSubalgebra.smul_mem _ c hy
  | lie y z hy' hz' hy hz =>
    rw [leibniz_lie]
    exact add_mem (LieSubalgebra.lie_mem _ hy hz') (LieSubalgebra.lie_mem _ hy' hz)

/-- The bracket of two elements of `𝔤' + H` lies in `𝔤'`, the image of Serre's presentation. -/
private theorem lie_mem_range_serreHom {x y : PresentedLieAlgebra R}
    (hx : x ∈ (serreHom R).range.toSubmodule ⊔ LinearMap.range (cartanElement R))
    (hy : y ∈ (serreHom R).range.toSubmodule ⊔ LinearMap.range (cartanElement R)) :
    ⁅x, y⁆ ∈ (serreHom R).range := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha, _, ⟨u, rfl⟩, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp hx
  obtain ⟨b, hb, _, ⟨v, rfl⟩, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp hy
  have hav : ⁅a, cartanElement R v⁆ ∈ (serreHom R).range := by
    rw [← lie_skew]
    exact neg_mem (lie_cartanElement_mem_range_serreHom R v ha)
  simp only [add_lie, lie_add, lie_cartanElement_cartanElement, add_zero]
  exact add_mem (add_mem (LieSubalgebra.lie_mem _ ha hb)
    (lie_cartanElement_mem_range_serreHom R u hb)) hav

/-- The Kac–Moody algebra is the sum of the image `𝔤'` of Serre's presentation and the Cartan
elements: `𝔤 = 𝔤' + H`. -/
theorem range_serreHom_sup_range_cartanElement :
    (serreHom R).range.toSubmodule ⊔ LinearMap.range (cartanElement R) = ⊤ := by
  rw [eq_top_iff]
  rintro z -
  have hz : z ∈ LieSubalgebra.lieSpan K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) (Set.range (cartanElement R) ∪
      Set.range (positiveGenerator R) ∪ Set.range (negativeGenerator R)) := by
    rw [lieSpan_generators_eq_top]
    trivial
  induction hz using LieSubalgebra.lieSpan_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    rcases hy with (⟨x, rfl⟩ | ⟨i, rfl⟩) | ⟨i, rfl⟩
    · exact Submodule.mem_sup_right ⟨x, rfl⟩
    · exact Submodule.mem_sup_left ⟨serreE K A i, serreHom_serreE R i⟩
    · exact Submodule.mem_sup_left ⟨serreF K A i, serreHom_serreF R i⟩
  | zero => exact zero_mem _
  | add y z _ _ hy hz => exact add_mem hy hz
  | smul c y _ hy => exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c hy
  | lie y z _ _ hy hz => exact Submodule.mem_sup_left (lie_mem_range_serreHom R hy hz)

/-- The image of Serre's presentation is the derived algebra `⁅𝔤, 𝔤⁆` of the Kac–Moody algebra. -/
theorem range_serreHom_eq_derivedSeries :
    (serreHom R).range =
      (derivedSeries K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) 1 : LieSubalgebra K (PresentedLieAlgebra R)) := by
  have hD : derivedSeries K (PresentedLieAlgebra R) 1 =
      ⁅(⊤ : LieIdeal K (PresentedLieAlgebra R)), ⊤⁆ := by
    rw [derivedSeries_def, derivedSeriesOfIdeal_succ, derivedSeriesOfIdeal_zero]
  refine le_antisymm ?_ fun y hy => ?_
  · rw [range_serreHom, LieSubalgebra.lieSpan_le, hD]
    rintro _ (⟨i, rfl⟩ | ⟨i, rfl⟩) <;>
      obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ : ∃ x, R.root i x = 1 := by
        obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := DFunLike.ne_iff.mp (R.root_linearIndependent.ne_zero i)
        exact ⟨(R.root i x)⁻¹ • x, by simpa using inv_mul_cancel₀ hx⟩
    · have h := lie_cartanElement_positiveGenerator R x i
      rw [hx, one_smul] at h
      rw [SetLike.mem_coe, LieIdeal.mem_toLieSubalgebra, ← h]
      exact LieSubmodule.lie_mem_lie trivial trivial
    · have h := lie_cartanElement_negativeGenerator R x i
      rw [hx, one_smul, ← neg_eq_iff_eq_neg] at h
      rw [SetLike.mem_coe, LieIdeal.mem_toLieSubalgebra, ← h]
      exact neg_mem (LieSubmodule.lie_mem_lie trivial trivial)
  · rw [LieIdeal.mem_toLieSubalgebra, hD, ← LieSubmodule.mem_toSubmodule,
      LieSubmodule.lieIdeal_oper_eq_linear_span'] at hy
    refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_ hy
    rintro _ ⟨a, -, b, -, rfl⟩
    have hsup := range_serreHom_sup_range_cartanElement R
    exact lie_mem_range_serreHom R (hsup ▸ Submodule.mem_top) (hsup ▸ Submodule.mem_top)

end Serre

section SerreCommutator

variable {R} {L : Type*} [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L] {φ : H →ₗ[K] L} {E F : I → L}

/-- For a generalized Cartan matrix, every `F k` commutes with each raising Serre element
`(ad (E i)) ^ (-Aᵢⱼ) ⁅E i, E j⁆`, as soon as `φ`, `E` and `F` satisfy the Chevalley
generator-bracket identities (Kac, §3.3). Neither Serre relation nor `[φ x, φ y] = 0` is used. -/
theorem lie_ad_pow_lie_eq_zero (hA : A.IsGeneralizedCartan)
    (hφE : ∀ x j, ⁅φ x, E j⁆ = R.root j x • E j)
    (hφF : ∀ x j, ⁅φ x, F j⁆ = -(R.root j x • F j))
    (hself : ∀ i, ⁅E i, F i⁆ = φ (R.coroot i))
    (hne : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → ⁅E i, F j⁆ = 0) (i j k : I) :
    ⁅F k, (ad K L (E i) ^ (-A i j).toNat) ⁅E i, E j⁆⁆ = 0 := by
  obtain rfl | hij := eq_or_ne i j
  · simp
  have hFE (a b : I) (hab : a ≠ b) : ⁅F b, E a⁆ = 0 := by
    rw [← lie_skew, hne a b hab, neg_zero]
  have hroot (a b : I) : R.root b (R.coroot a) = (A a b : K) := by simp
  rw [← ad_pow_succ_apply]
  obtain rfl | hki := eq_or_ne k i
  · by_cases h0 : φ (R.coroot k) = 0
    · rw [TauCeti.LieAlgebra.lie_ad_pow_of_lie_eq_zero
          (by rw [← lie_skew, hself, h0, neg_zero]),
        hFE j k hij.symm, map_zero]
    have t : IsSl2Triple (φ (R.coroot k)) (E k) (F k) :=
      { h_ne_zero := h0
        lie_e_f := hself k
        lie_h_e_nsmul := by rw [hφE, hroot, hA.diag]; simp [two_smul]
        lie_h_f_nsmul := by rw [hφF, hroot, hA.diag]; simp [two_smul] }
    have hstring := t.lie_f_pow_succ_toEnd_e (y := E j) (μ := (A k j : K))
      (by rw [hφE, hroot]) (hFE j k hij.symm) (-A k j).toNat
    rw [← ad_eq_toEnd] at hstring
    rw [hstring]
    have hn : (((-A k j).toNat : ℕ) : K) = -(A k j : K) := by
      rw [← Int.cast_natCast, Int.toNat_of_nonneg (by linarith [hA.offDiag_nonpos k j hij]),
        Int.cast_neg]
    rw [hn, sub_neg_eq_add, neg_add_cancel, mul_zero, zero_smul]
  rw [TauCeti.LieAlgebra.lie_ad_pow_of_lie_eq_zero (hFE i k hki.symm)]
  obtain rfl | hkj := eq_or_ne k j
  · rw [← lie_skew, hself, pow_succ, mul_apply_eq_comp, map_neg, ad_apply,
      lie_skew, hφE, hroot]
    rcases h_neg : (-A i k).toNat with _ | n
    · have hik : A i k = 0 := le_antisymm (hA.offDiag_nonpos i k hij) (by omega)
      simp [(hA.zero_comm i k).mp hik]
    · rw [map_smul, pow_succ, mul_apply_eq_comp, ad_apply, lie_self, map_zero, smul_zero]
  · rw [hFE j k hkj.symm, map_zero]

end SerreCommutator

